SUMMARY:Klidonas\, Houdetsi
LOCATION:Houdetsi\, Crete (Heraklion)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Peza wine village revives the St John's Eve custom properly: on the afternoon of 23 June the May wreaths are burned and people jump the bonfire three times\, the 'silent water' is fetched and the girls' fortunes read\, then Cretan music in the square with free entry (Kakoudakis and Petsakis in 2025). Houdetsi is 20 km south of Heraklion\; the Erotokritos cultural workshop organises it.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/heraklion/#houdetsi-klidonas-houdetsi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/heraklion/#houdetsi-klidonas-houdetsi
